  "body": "Both GNOME Terminal and Ptyxis (as of 48.alpha) have buttons in their Preferences dialog to set as default terminal. I think it's expected that when a user clicks that button for the change to take effect. If I understand the cache correctly, that won't work unless the apps explicitly clear the cache.  And I guess to clear the cache, the app needs to remove the user's cache file themselves.\n\nI suggest that the cache feature be disabled by default.",
